            "title": "Incorrect error callback invocation on successful sendFile with HEAD/304",
            "severity": "medium",
            "file": "lib/response.js",
            "line": 912,
            "explanation": "The 'sendfile' function added code registers an 'onerror' listener with onFinished for the response object but uses the 'onfinish' callback for file 'file' event. Previously, 'onfinish' was directly used for onFinished. Also, the onfinish function unconditionally calls callback with an error if streaming is true, even if the status code is 304 or the request method is HEAD, which should be considered a normal scenario and not an error. This causes the callback to be called with a 'Request aborte",
            "suggestion": "Modify the 'onfinish' function to check if the response status code is 304 or if the request method is HEAD and streaming is true, then call callback without error. Only call callback with error for other premature close cases.",
            "failureAfterChange": "When calling res.sendFile() with a HEAD request or after a conditional GET with 304 Not Modified response, the callback is invoked with an error 'Request aborted' although the operation was successful.",
            "alreadyFixedByChange": false
          }
        ],
